{title: I Believe In The Cross}
{key: F}

{comment: Chorus}
[F]I believe in the cross. I believe in the [Bb]cleansing blood.
I believe in a [C]hill called Calvary where Jesus [Bb]died for you and [F]me.
I believe that He lives, and that He's [Bb]coming [A]back a[Gm]gain
Every [C]knee shall bow and every tongue confess - this I be[F]lieve.

{comment: Verse 1}
I be[F]lieve He was born in a manger bed as the [Bb]star shone bright that [F]night
[C]Wise men came to worship Him with their [Bb]gifts of pure de[F]light
I be[F]lieve He was born of a virgin birth - mira[A]culous, it's [Dm]true.
I be[G]lieve this lowly child grew up to be the De[C]liverer for me and you.

{comment: Verse 2}
I be[F]lieve He has the power to heal the sick, cause the [Bb]blinded eyes to [F]see.
I be[C]lieve all Hell has to lose it's hold when He [Bb]sets the demoniac [F]free.
I be[F]lieve that He walked on the water, and he mul[A]tiplied food to [Dm]eat.
I be[G]lieve that he's given me the power to use his [C]name with authority.

{comment: Bridge}
[F]Oh the blood of Jesus, oh, the [C]blood of Je[F]sus.
[F]Oh the blood of Jesus - it wa[Bb]shes  [C]white as [F]snow.
